Package: uu-remote-for-linux
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: UU Remote for Linux Contributors
Depends: bash, ca-certificates, coreutils, curl, ethtool, findutils, gir1.2-appindicator3-0.1, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gstreamer1.0-pipewire, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, iproute2, libglib2.0-bin, libx11-6, libxtst6, network-manager, policykit-1, python3, python3-gi, systemd, tar, util-linux, xdg-desktop-portal, zenity
Recommends: wine (>= 11.1) | winehq-stable (>= 11.1) | winehq-devel (>= 11.1) | winehq-staging (>= 11.1), libnotify-bin, pciutils
Suggests: vainfo
Description: unofficial UU Remote compatibility wrapper for Linux
 Runs the official NetEase UU Remote Windows client in an isolated Wine prefix
 with native Linux integration for controller and X11 or Portal-bridged Wayland
 controlled-host workflows, including optional NVIDIA NVDEC decoding and NVENC
 H.264/HEVC encoding bridges. The proprietary upstream installer is downloaded
 from NetEase on first setup and is not included in this package.
